// Gen IV (Diamond, Pearl, Platinum, HeartGold, SoulSilver) PK4 legality through
// Legality::analyzePk4 and through Legality::analyze, which folds the Gen IV analyzer
// into its report for a native PK4 (Legality::applyGen4Analyzer).
//
// Fixture records are synthetic: PKHeX.Core (commit pinned in Gen4LegalityData.h)
// built each one from its own encounter templates for a test trainer "Tester"
// (tools/pkhex_gen34_diff, `generate 1 3 4 base|grown`), and some carry the single-
// field mutation the oracle applied. The game id names the save that holds the record;
// PKHeX judged each record with that game's personal table. Expected verdict classes:
//   Valid    PKHeX VALID; NoProblemsFound here (every coverage area Complete).
//   Invalid  PKHeX INVALID and Invalid here.
//   Unknown  PKHeX VALID with a Fishy (Warning) result, or a Pal Park transfer from
//            Colosseum/XD: Warning and Incomplete here, never Invalid. Three Fishy results
//            that normal play produces (EffortEXPIncreased, Effort2Remaining,
//            LevelEXPThreshold) are Info here, so such a record is Valid.
// Pal Park transfers from R/S/E/FR/LG are verified against the Gen III encounter tables.
// Then one hand-made negative per verified rule (each also run through PKHeX, whose
// result is noted next to it), malformed sizes, checksum and sanity failures, the hook
// merge rules, input immutability and a deterministic fuzz pass over random and mutated
// records (run under ASan/UBSan by host-sanitize).
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cstddef>
